Check for private endpoint access to the Kubernetes API server Internal Only - General
oci ce cluster get \
--cluster-id $CLUSTER_ID \
--query 'data.{endpointConfig:"endpoint-config",endpoints:endpoints}' \
--output json
Expected Output:
{
"endpointConfig": {
"is-public-ip-enabled": false,
"nsg-ids": [
"ocid1.networksecuritygroup.oc1..."
],
"subnet-id": "ocid1.subnet.oc1..."
},
"endpoints": {
"private-endpoint": "10.0.0.10:6443",
"public-endpoint": null
}
}
Confirm that is-public-ip-enabled is false, private-endpoint is populated, and public-endpoint is null. If is-public-ip-enabled is true or public-endpoint contains a value, public IP access is enabled and the cluster does not meet this control.
